From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:13:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/52] Parse the symbol attributes of KiCad 10 rule areas

KiCad 10 rule areas can override the DNP, simulation, BOM and board
attributes of the symbols inside them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013wvKon1yvwjNtAdtSuZzZh
---
 src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic.py | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic.py b/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic.py
index 0736ecb..60971ba 100644
--- a/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic.py
+++ b/src/gerbonara/cad/kicad/schematic.py
@@ -628,6 +628,11 @@ class Subsheet:
 
 @sexp_type('rule_area')
 class RuleArea:
+    # KiCad 10 lets rule areas set these attributes of the symbols inside them.
+    exclude_from_sim: Named(YesNoAtom()) = None
+    in_bom: Named(YesNoAtom()) = None
+    on_board: Named(YesNoAtom()) = None
+    dnp: Named(YesNoAtom()) = None
     polyline: Polyline = None
 
 
